===BODY===
          <h2>What can usually be fixed at the roadside</h2>
          <ul>
            <li><strong>Flat batteries:</strong> a jump start to get you going, then advice on whether the battery or charging system needs checking. See <a href="{{R}}guides/flat-battery-jump-start-or-recovery.html">jump start or recovery?</a></li>
            <li><strong>Punctures:</strong> fitting your spare wheel, if you have a usable one and the car can be safely jacked up where it's parked.</li>
            <li><strong>Simple starting problems:</strong> things like a key fob with a dead battery or a steering lock that won't release.</li>
          </ul>

          <h2>When roadside help isn't the answer</h2>
          <p>Some problems can't, or shouldn't, be fixed at the side of the road: an engine or gearbox fault, a car that's been <a href="{{R}}guides/wrong-fuel.html">misfuelled</a>, a puncture without a usable spare, or anything after an accident. In those cases we'll recover the car to a garage or your home instead, <strong>from £125</strong>, and we'll tell you that before anyone sets off, so you're not paying for a visit that can't fix the problem.</p>

          <div class="callout">
            <p><strong>On a motorway, safety comes first.</strong> Roadside repairs aren't done in a live lane or on a busy hard shoulder. If you've stopped on a fast road, get behind the barrier and call. The car will normally be taken somewhere safe before anything else.</p>
          </div>

          <h2>Describe the symptoms</h2>
          <p>The more you can tell us, the better we can judge whether a roadside fix will work: what noise the car makes when you try to start it, which warning lights are on, whether it stopped suddenly or lost power gradually. A quick video on WhatsApp is often the most useful thing you can send.</p>
===FAQ===
Q: Can you jump start my car?
A: If the problem is a flat battery, usually yes. Tell us the symptoms and we'll tell you whether a jump start is likely to work, or whether the car needs a garage.
Q: Can you change my tyre?
A: If you have a usable spare and the car is parked somewhere it can be safely jacked up, yes. If there's no spare, or only a repair kit that won't work, we'll recover the car to a tyre fitter or garage.
Q: What if the roadside fix doesn't work?
A: Then the car is recovered to a garage or your home instead. We'll explain the options and the price before anything is done.
